## REDIS OVERVIEW
=====================

Redis ek fast, in-memory data store hai jo
primarily data ko RAM (memory) me store karta hai.

Redis ka primary working data RAM me hota hai,
lekin Redis durability / recovery ke liye
data ko disk par persist bhi kar sakta hai.


## REDIS AS A CACHE
-------------------

Caching ke context me Redis ko ek dedicated
external cache ke roop me use kiya ja sakta hai.

Ye Application aur Database ke beech
ek fast-access data layer provide karta hai.


Application
     |
     ↓
   Redis
  (Cache)
     |
     ↓
 Database


## KEY-VALUE MODEL
-------------------

Redis fundamentally key-value data model provide karta hai.

Example:

    Key:
        product:101

    Value:
        {
            "id": 101,
            "name": "iPhone",
            "price": 79999
        }


Application:

    GET product:101
            ↓
          Redis
            ↓
    Corresponding Value


## TTL (TIME TO LIVE)
---------------------

Redis keys ke saath TTL (Time To Live) set kiya ja sakta hai.

Example:

    product:101
        ↓
    TTL = 10 minutes


TTL expire hone ke baad key available nahi rahegi.

Agar usi key ke liye next request aaye,
to data cache me available nahi hoga.

Application Database se fresh data retrieve karegi,
usse Redis me dobara cache karegi,
aur client ko response return karegi.

Example:

    Request
       ↓
    Redis
       ↓
    Key Not Found
       ↓
    Database
       ↓
    Fresh Data


===============================
## CACHE HIT vs CACHE MISS
===============================

## CACHE HIT
-------------

Jab application requested data ko Cache me
successfully find kar leti hai, to ise Cache Hit kehte hain.

Is case me application directly Cache se data retrieve
karke response return kar deti hai, aur Database ko
hit karne ki zarurat nahi padti.


## CACHE MISS
--------------

Jab requested data Cache me available nahi hota,
to ise Cache Miss kehte hain.

Is case me application Database se data retrieve karti hai,
use future requests ke liye Cache me store karti hai,
aur phir response return karti hai.


